  "emailBody": "\n        <html>\n\n        <body\n            style=\"\n                font-family:Segoe UI, Arial, sans-serif;\n                margin:20px;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    background:#d42e12;\n                    color:white;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                \"\n            >\n\n\n               <h1 style=\"margin:0;\">\n                    Fuel Market Intelligence Morning Report\n                </h1>\n\n                <p style=\"margin:5px 0 0 0;\">\n                    26 August 2026\n                </p>\n\n            </div>\n\n            <p\n                style=\"\n                    font-size:16px;\n                    margin-top:20px;\n                    margin-bottom:20px;\n                \"\n            >\n                Good morning Sir,\n                <br><br>\n                \n                Here is today's fuel market intelligence report highlighting\n                the latest PMS and AGO depot prices together with key industry\n                developments and market news.\n            </p>\n\n            <br>\n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            PMS Prices\n        </h2>\n\n        <div\n            style=\"\n                background:#fad5a1;\n                padding:12px;\n                border-left:5px solid #f28e05;\n                margin-bottom:10px;\n                font-size:16px;\n                font-weight:bold;\n            \"\n        >\n            Average PMS Prices: ₦1,201.62/L\n        </div>\n\n        <table\n            width=\"100%\"\n            cellspacing=\"0\"\n            cellpadding=\"10\"\n            style=\"\n                border-collapse:collapse;\n                border:1px solid #ddd;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <tr style=\"background:#d42e12;color:white;\">\n                <th align=\"left\">Depot</th>\n                <th align=\"left\">Price</th>\n            </tr>\n\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DANGOTE</td>\n                <td>₦1,200.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>PINNACLE</td>\n                <td>₦1,186.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MRS TINCAN</td>\n                <td>₦1,192.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>RAINOIL DELTA</td>\n                <td>₦1,215.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>NEPAL</td>\n                <td>₦1,215.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>INTERGRATED</td>\n                <td>₦1,195.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AFRICAN TERMINAL</td>\n                <td>₦1,195.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>FYNEFIELD</td>\n                <td>₦1,215.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            AGO Prices\n        </h2>\n\n        <div\n            style=\"\n                background:#fad5a1;\n                padding:12px;\n                border-left:5px solid #f28e05;\n                margin-bottom:10px;\n                font-size:16px;\n                font-weight:bold;\n            \"\n        >\n            Average AGO Prices: ₦1,680.62/L\n        </div>\n\n        <table\n            width=\"100%\"\n            cellspacing=\"0\"\n            cellpadding=\"10\"\n            style=\"\n                border-collapse:collapse;\n                border:1px solid #ddd;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <tr style=\"background:#d42e12;color:white;\">\n                <th align=\"left\">Depot</th>\n                <th align=\"left\">Price</th>\n            </tr>\n\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>RAINOIL DELTA</td>\n                <td>₦1,730.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>SAHARA</td>\n                <td>₦1,670.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DUPORT</td>\n                <td>₦1,670.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>TMDK</td>\n                <td>₦1,675.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>WOSBAB</td>\n                <td>₦1,675.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MENJ</td>\n                <td>₦1,675.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBACHEM</td>\n                <td>₦1,675.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>T.TIME</td>\n                <td>₦1,675.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Oil Prices Fall Nearly 8% in Two Days as U.S.-Iran Tensions Ease\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Brent crude was trading at $86.44 per barrel, down 2.42 per cent, as at 05:30am (WAT) on Wednesday. West Texas Intermediate stood at $80.54, down2.21 per cent. The reversal reflects a sharp unwinding of the geopolitical risk premium that had driven Brent towards $95 per barrel. The slide reflects easing fears that the US-Iran confrontation would escalate.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/oil-prices-fall-nearly-8-in-two-days-as-us-iran-tensions-ease\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    JUST IN: Dangote Refinery Raises Petrol Gantry Price to ₦1,200/Litre\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Dangote Petroleum Refinery has raised its Premium Motor Spirit (PMS) gantry price by ₦15 per litre. The latest adjustment marks the second PMS price increase by the refinery within seven days. The development is expected to put fresh upward pressure on the downstream market.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/just-in-dangote-refinery-raises-petrol-gantry-price-to-1200litre\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Oil Prices Fall Nearly 4% as Iran Negotiation Hopes Return\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Brent crude had declined $3.41, or 3.70%, to $88.76 a barrel, while U.S. West Texas Intermediate (WTI) fell $2.89, or 4.40%, to £82.12 a barrel. The decline came as markets responded to signs that diplomatic efforts could reopen a path towards negotiations with Tehran.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/oil-prices-fall-nearly-4-as-iran-negotiation-hopes-return\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    China, Iraq, Turkey Face Mounting Risks as Trump Tightens Iran Sanctions\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The next phase of the Trump administration’s economic offensive against Iran is shifting the pressure from Tehran itself to the countries that continue to sustain its oil, gas and commercial lifelines. China, Iraq, Turkey, India and the United Arab Emirates face different degrees of exposure. Washington threatens to expand secondary sanctions against businesses, financial institutions and intermediaries dealing with Iran.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/china-iraq-turkey-face-mounting-risks-as-trump-tightens-iran-sanctions\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Petrol, LPG Stock Levels Fall Below 30-Day Sufficiency Threshold\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigeria’s petrol and liquefied petroleum gas (LPG) inventories fell below the 30-day minimum fuel sufficiency threshold in July 2026. The shortfall was not reflected across all major petroleum products. Petrol remains the largest of the four key products by daily consumption.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/petrol-lpg-stock-levels-fall-below-30-day-sufficiency-threshold\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
